se},"event":"unlabeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2017-07-18T14:31:45Z","label":{"name":"need more info","color":"5319e7"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/316083953","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/3079#issuecomment-316083953","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/3079","id":316083953,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMxNjA4Mzk1Mw==","user":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-07-18T14:35:42Z","updated_at":"2017-07-18T14:35:42Z","body":"Figured it out; ignore me :). This is an interesting bug. We do correctly discard and re-buffer a different format if the track selector indicates that a different stream should be selected after preparation completes, and the decoder doesn't ever receive an input buffer in the discarded format.\r\n\r\nThere is however a separate optimization that's supposed to allow the format to be delivered to the decoder a little sooner, and this optimization is allowing the format of the discarded media to be delivered to the decoder.\r\n\r\nWe'll get that fixed. Note that once it's fixed, it's probably the case that you'll no longer need to do anything manual in your application code to restrict the streams that are being selected. The default track selection logic is supposed to do this automatically.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/316083953/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/316085400","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/3079#issuecomment-316085400","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/3079","id":316085400,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMxNjA4NTQwMA==","user":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-07-18T14:40:09Z","updated_at":"2017-07-18T14:40:57Z","body":"As an aside for producing your streams: HLS players typically download a segment of the first variant listed in the master playlist at the start of playback. So you shouldn't put the highest quality variant first. [Apple's best practices](https://developer.apple.com/library/content/technotes/tn2224/_index.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/DTS40009745-CH1-BITRATERECOMMENDATIONS) state:\r\n\r\n> The first entry in the master playlist will be played at the initiation of a stream and is used as part of a test to determine which stream is most appropriate. The order of the other streams is irrelevant. Therefore, the first bit rate in the playlist should be the one that most clients can sustain.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/316085400/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/316088394","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/3079#issuecomment-316088394","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/3079","id":316088394,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMxNjA4ODM5NA==","user":{"login":"davibe","id":123929,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzkyOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123929?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibe","html_url":"https://github.com/davibe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-07-18T14:49:23Z","updated_at":"2017-07-18T14:55:05Z","body":"You are right, I am sorry I was not very precise while addressing th